			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add extensionGalleryManifest stub and stub-hit disposition tracking\n\nAdd IPC stub for `extensionGalleryManifest` channel to support workbench's `setExtensionGalleryManifest({...})` call at boot. Also add `__initialize` to the playwright stub object.\n\nEnhance stub-hit logging to track disposition: `value` for real payloads, `noop` for intentionally undefined stubs, and `drift` for keys missing from the stub object (potential sync issue between Wind and Output bundles). Uses `Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call()` for reliable property checking.\n\nThis continues the channel-stub forensic work from recent releases, ensuring Wind's stub definitions stay lockstep with Output bundle IPC surface.",
			"SHA": "5e66b9dcfb91db3b54be0e9d57b36248b521cf5f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T17:24:31Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1049,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add localGit IPC routing and tauri-invoke timing instrumentation\n\n- Route `localGit` channel to Mountain's `git:*` subprocess handlers, enabling VS Code's built-in git extension to work with Land's native git implementation\n- Wrap InvokeMountain with per-invoke timing instrumentation that logs ok/fail and elapsed_ms to the dev-log sink, helping distinguish webview transport latency from Mountain handler slowness (Echo backlog, lock contention)\n- Add Batch 6 IPC stubs for VS Code shared-process services: test, profileStorageListener, checksum, languagePacks, userDataSyncUtil, userDataSyncMachines, IUserDataSyncResourceProviderService, customEndpointTelemetry, process, remoteTunnel, sharedWebContentExtractor, playwright, v8InspectProfiling\n- Add preload-shim diagnostic logging that surfaces which global keys are installed when running in Tauri vs non-Tauri hosts\n\nThese changes enable the built-in git extension to function while providing granular visibility into IPC latency.",
			"SHA": "d719605247cc7deacc5072f13ce89b46f947bfda"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T16:53:32Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1049,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Wind): Add IPC stubs for telemetryAppender and mcpGalleryManifest\n\nAdd no-op stubs for two high-frequency IPC channels that were causing\nunnecessary Tauri round-trips:\n\n- `telemetryAppender`: VS Code's TelemetryChannelAppender posts every\nevent through the shared-process channel. Land has no shared process or\ntelemetry backend, so each call fell through to\n`InvokeMountain(\"undefined:log\")`. Observed at 155 calls per boot in\n`channel-stub` tag output - by far the hottest miss. The stub provides\n`log`/`flush` no-ops so the appender short-circuits in the stub path.\n\n- `mcpGalleryManifest`: MCP extension marketplace manifest bootstrap.\n`channel-stub` surfaced this as the sole remaining `miss` per session.\nThe workbench calls `setMcpGalleryManifest({...})` once at boot; a no-op\nstub is sufficient until Land has an MCP registry.\n\nAlso enhance `_DevLogForward` to send both casings (Tag/Message AND\ntag/message) so Tauri's param-case handling doesn't require a guess -\nthe Rust command coalesces whichever arrived populated. Add fallback to\n`__TAURI_INTERNALS__` for broader Tauri version compatibility.\n\nImpact: Eliminates ~156 unnecessary Tauri IPC round-trips per editor\nboot, reducing startup latency.",
			"SHA": "1d3e91dfe93e57f23ed5c4e350621a73ae5082b8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T15:56:31Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1049,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add dev-log forwarding from TypeScript to Mountain\n\nAdd a _DevLogForward helper that mirrors tagged log lines into Mountain's dev-log file sink via the RenderDevLog Tauri command. Integrate it into TauriChannel's three code paths:\n- Fire-and-forget channel invocations\n- Stub hits (when a mocked response is used)\n- Misses (when neither route nor stub exists)\n\nThis enables `LAND_DEV_LOG=<tag> tail -f Mountain.dev.log` to capture TypeScript-originated IPC traffic alongside Rust dev_log! output for better local development debugging.",
			"SHA": "d7daf83f6c42a66a4bf4522b293cd96014549d8f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T15:31:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1049,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Wind): Remove deprecated IPC channels and add diagnostics stub\n\nConsolidate SkyEvent channels onto canonical kebab-case forms:\n- Remove StatusBarMessage (fork of StatusBarSetMessage)\n- Remove TreeViewRegister (fork of TreeViewCreate)\n- Remove WebviewPostMessageCamelCase / WebviewSetHTMLCamelCase (forks)\n\nAdd diagnostics stub to prevent TypeError in language detection. The\nlanguageDetectionWorkerServiceImpl synchronously calls\ngetWorkspaceFileExtensions which returns undefined without a stub,\ncausing 'undefined is not an object' when iterating extensions.\n\nThe stub returns empty shapes matching the expected interface, allowing\nlanguage detection to proceed without workspace-derived biases.",
			"SHA": "1e943100e0bdd74a1a17933f7e4ead2e33f7a3b6"
		}
	],
